01:01:25,714 --> 01:01:31,714
Dead Poets Society is a 1989 American coming-of-age drama film
directed by Peter Weir and written by Tom Schulman.

11
01:07:34,285 --> 01:07:40,285
The film, starring Robin Williams, is set in 1959 at a
fictional elite boarding school called Welton Academy.

12
01:13:42,857 --> 01:13:48,857
It tells the story of an English teacher who inspires his
students through his teaching of poetry.

13
01:19:51,428 --> 01:19:57,428
Dead Poets Society was produced by Touchstone Pictures and Silver Screen Partners IV and
released in the United States by Buena Vista Pictures Distribution on June 2, 1989.

14
01:26:00,000 --> 01:26:06,000
The film was a commercial success and received critical acclaim.

15
01:32:08,571 --> 01:32:14,571
It grossed $235.9 million worldwide against a $16.4 million budget,
becoming the fifth-highest-grossing film of 1989.

16
01:38:17,142 --> 01:38:23,142
The film received numerous accolades, including Academy Award nominations for Best
Picture and Best Director and a Best Actor nomination for Williams.

17
01:44:25,714 --> 01:44:31,714
The film won the BAFTA Award for Best Film, the César Award for Best Foreign
Film and the David di Donatello Award for Best Foreign Film.

18
01:50:34,285 --> 01:50:40,285
Schulman received the Academy Award for Best Original Screenplay for his work.

19
01:56:42,857 --> 01:56:48,857
The film explores themes of individual,
friendship, philosophy, poetry, literature.

20
02:02:51,428 --> 02:02:57,428
The tone is lighthearted and emotional and intense.
